  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services obligated $802M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services won 258 awards this fiscal year to date and had an average award size of $3.1M, with obligations down 42.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $727M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $42.7M and the Department of Justice at $25.7M. Engineering Services is the largest market for Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services, accounting for $600M in obligations, with Computer Systems Design Services next at $108M. Other notable markets include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $41.3M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $28M. Historical context shows higher annual obligations in prior years, including $1B in FY21 and $1.4B in both FY24 and FY25, which highlights the concentration of current work with a few large agencies and markets.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers for Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $727M from Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $42.7M and the Department of Justice obligated $25.7M. The Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation obligated $3.5M and the Department of Labor obligated $4.4M, while the National Aeronautics and Space Administration shows $0 for this period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and services drive Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for Bae Systems Technology Solutions and Services at $600M in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services contributed $108M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing contributed $41.3M. Smaller markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $28M and Other Computer Related Services at $14.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
